 "about": "JUN-364: capability refusals are named before the runtime traps. Each case is a guest whose one capability call the runtime refuses. Natively (seed/76, seed/77) the image runs with KEXE_ALLOW=allow, KEXE_CAP_RESOURCES_35 = the run directory (which holds refusal-in.txt, 4 bytes) as the working directory, and must exit 120 with stderr exactly `stderr` followed by the trap line KEXE_TRAP {:kind :signal :signal :SIGILL}. As a wasm32-browser module (seed/82) the page grants wasm32.allow and the run must exit 120 with wasm32.stderr followed by the same trap line.",
